//! The surface table, as the game builds it: `SurfaceTable_Init` 0x256188 fills 20 rows of 25 words (100 bytes a
//! row, the pointer in $a0) for the 20 surface types a patch or object can carry (rider+0x290 picks the row).
//! Every word below was read out of the original by running it in the function runner (row E8f), and
//! `tests/surface_table.rs` checks them bit for bit against it.
//!
//! Units are the game's: cm, cm/s², degrees, km/h. What a column is used for (proven: read from the code that
//! reads it; inferred: a guess), by word offset in the row:
//! - +0x00 [0] gravity, cm/s² (proven, `Boarder_GroundSpringForce` 0x109878)
//! - +0x04..+0x0c [1..3] drag: linear, square, cube (proven, `Boarder_ForwardDrag` 0x109cb8)
//! - +0x10 [4] side grip (proven, `Boarder_SideFriction` 0x109ef8)
//! - +0x14 [5] most lean, degrees (port-notes/boarder.md)
//! - +0x18 [6] height above the snow, cm, past which the board is in the air (port-notes/boarder.md)
//! - +0x1c, +0x20 [7, 8] the ground spring's band d1, d2, cm (proven, `Boarder_GroundSpringForce` reads
//!   rider+0x294/+0x298, which ease toward these)
//! - +0x24 [9] normal damping, 1/s (proven, `Boarder_GroundSpringForce`)
//! - +0x2c [11] speed the rider pushes himself to, km/h; +0x30 [12] thrust scale (proven, `Boarder_GroundThrust`
//!   0x109950)
//! - +0x34..+0x40 [13..16] spray: rate factor, flake size cm, two life times s (port-notes/effects.md, spray.rs)
//! - [10], [18..20], [22..24]: floats not yet traced; [17] and [21] are integers (written with `sw`)

